# TWO DISTINCT operands. cpu_mul/cpu_vmul use `v .* v`, where both reads hit
# one buffer -- that halves the memory traffic and could flatter or penalise
# either path unevenly. This variant streams two separate arrays, which is
# what real elementwise code does.
v = reshape(randn(4000000, 1), 2000, 2000)
w = reshape(randn(4000000, 1), 2000, 2000)
x = v .* w
for r = 1 to 60
    x = v .* w
end for
print("done")
